From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Druchenko <bananos@dev.co.ua>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:01:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] b43: N-PHY: 802.11n at 20 MHz on radio 2057 rev 13
 (experimental)

Optionally (module parameter ht=1, off by default) announce HT on the
2.4 GHz band of N-PHY rev 17 with radio 2057 rev 13 (BCM5357/53572,
ASUS RT-N12 D1), the one PHY it was tested on, and send and receive
MCS 0-15 at 20 MHz: no A-MPDU, no short guard interval. ht=2 sends one
stream only.

TX (v4 firmware header, 598 format): the HT-SIG as the PLCP, the
mixed-mode L-SIG length, HT encoding, the MCS's modulation and coding
and the stream mode (CDD for one stream, SDM for two) in PHY control 1,
an MCS or legacy fallback, and the NAV, which mac80211 leaves to the
driver for MCS rates. HT frames go without RTS/CTS for now.

RX: the PLCP of an HT frame is its HT-SIG (MCS, 40 MHz, short GI). This
PHY reports HT frames as type 2 (PRE_N), so both N types are taken.

Off by default: on the RT-N12 D1 most HT frames need retries (TX
calibration and power control for this radio are not derived yet), and
throughput (11-12 Mbit/s each way) does not beat 802.11g so far.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
